\title{glyanno: Hierarchical Glycan Annotation}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Hierarchical annotation of glycans based on molecule mass, composition, and structure. Starting from a molecule mass, glyanno calculates possible glycan compositions. Given a glycan composition, glyanno further deduces possible glycan structures. For glycan structures with generic monosaccharides (e.g., "Hex", "HexNAc"), glyanno refines them into specific types (e.g., "Glc", "Gal"). For structures lacking linkage information (e.g., "Gal(??-?)GalNAc(??-"), glyanno infers the most likely linkages (e.g., "Gal(b1-3)GalNAc(a1-").
}
